# TD-MPC2 H=6 fleet — run with
#   supervisor.py --queue scripts/tdmpc/h6_queue.jsonl --run_tag h6 --grade_plant baseline
#     --grade_horizon 6 --grade_warm_start --max_env_steps 3000000 --min_judge_steps 2000000
#
# WHY (measured 2026-08-13, fidelity audit vs tdmpc2_official + the honest fall metric):
#   Planning at H=6 instead of H=3 on ALREADY-TRAINED checkpoints removes 12.5-18.7 pp of the
#   episode fall rate, on all three walkers tested, with tilt DOWN and speed UP. No weight in the
#   world model depends on horizon, so that was free. H=3 = 0.12 s of lookahead against a ~0.7 s
#   gait cycle; the planner could not see a fall coming. H=12 buys nothing further and costs speed,
#   so the learned dynamics are good to ~0.25 s and no further.
#
# THE QUESTION THIS FLEET ANSWERS: does TRAINING at H=6 beat PLANNING at H=6 with an H=3-trained
# model? It should -- the consistency loss would fit 6-step rollouts and the value function would
# match the horizon actually used -- but that is a hypothesis, not a measurement.
#
# BASELINE TO BEAT (lean-C, trained H=3, planned at H=6, graded with objective walk_v2):
#   fitness 0.0807 | falls 18.8% of episodes | tilt 9.1 deg | lean -3.9 | fwd 0.312 (1.04x cmd)
#   PPO reference: fitness 0.2571 | falls 6.2% | tilt 9.7 | fwd 0.281
# Every arm is lean-C's exact recipe (soft gate 0.95/0.15, demo-anchored buffer, bc_plan_std 0.15,
# 400k seed, 20k pretrain, baseline plant, fixed cmd 0.3) PLUS --horizon 6 --mppi_warm_start, so
# the H=3-vs-H=6 comparison is single-variable against a policy we have already measured.
#
# COST: MPPI is linear in H, so collection runs ~2x slower than the lean fleet -- expect ~8 h/arm,
# ~33 h total. Arms are ordered so the primary question is answered first; stopping after idx 1
# still yields the answer plus its replicate.
#
# GRADING: objective walk_v2 (fitness = track * safety * (0.6*posture + 0.4*smooth)), which has
# 21.4x dynamic range across our real policies where v1 had 1.01x. Win bar: fwd>=0.25,
# |lean|<=15 deg, AND pct_episodes_with_fall <= 10%. Nothing we have trained passes it yet.
